579 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 257 0 R
/E (Pistons won and lost the turnover battle. This suggests that turnover percentage alone was not a primary driver of game outcomes. Instead, the impact of turnovers was highly context-dependent. Many of the most damaging turnovers occurred in already-losing game states, particularly live-ball turnovers from primary ball handlers that led directly to opponent fast-break opportunities. In these situations, turnovers functioned less as the cause of losses and more as an accelerant, widening margins by fueling transition scoring and preventing Detroit from leveraging its half-court defensive structure. Compared to shooting efficiency, which influences nearly every possession, turnovers affected outcomes unevenly based on timing, location, and game flow.)
/Pg 39 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
580 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
